  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\axiom.of.union]\nAxiom:\ngiven: X is \\set\nthen:\n. exists: U is \\set\n  suchThat:\n  . forAll: Z is \\set\n    then:\n    . have: Z \"in\" U\n      iff:\n      . exists: W is \\set\n        suchThat:\n        . W \"in\"? X\n        . Z \"in\"? W\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Axiom of Union\"\n. description: \"For a set $X$ whose members are themselves sets, there is a set\n                $U$ containing exactly those $Z$ that belong to some member $W$\n                of $X$. It flattens one level of nesting, combining the elements\n                of all the members of $X$.\"\nId: \"60bcea09-6bf1-4917-b90f-64ceeb941558\"",
